    <!-- v5/PhaseA: STAGING NEST. A cleaned part is set down here and re-gripped
         by its BODY -- the cap grip only survives a short carry (see PAIN_JOURNAL).
         BORE IS SIZED TO THE LUGS, NOT THE BODY: the bayonet lugs stick out to r=34mm
         while the body is only r=21.5mm. A 27mm bore (5.5mm body clearance) was tried
         first and interfered with the lugs by exactly 7.0mm; the solver resolved that
         by launching the part back out. Bore is now r=38mm = 4mm lug clearance.
         The wide bore does not let the part lean: a 110mm cylinder on a flat 43mm
         base is self-standing (it only topples past ~21deg), so the walls just stop
         it wandering and the 45-degree lead-in funnels it in.
